\f1\b\fs84 \cf3 Vector Database: What is it and why you should know it?
\f0\b0\fs24 \cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b\fs40 \cf3 \'93If 2021 was the year of graph databases, 2023 is the year of vector databases\'94 \'97\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://huyenchip.com/"}}{\fldrslt \ul Chip Huen}}.
\f3\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\i0 \cf3 Why? you ask...\
Well, it\'92s because\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.techtarget.com/searchenterpriseai/definition/generative-AI"}}{\fldrslt \ul Generative AI}}\'a0and\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://machinelearningmastery.com/what-are-large-language-models/"}}{\fldrslt \ul Large Language Models (LLMs)}}\'a0are now popular and one of the best ways to handle LLM data is with a vector database because vector databases provide the ideal infrastructure for managing the complex, high-dimensional data that LLMs produce and thrive on.\
In this article, we\'92ll discuss what vector databases are, how they work, and some excellent vector database tools you should check out.\
Before we dive into vector databases, let\'92s first understand what a vector is.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf3 What is a Vector?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\b0\fs40 \cf3 In machine learning (ML), a vector is a collection of numerical values that represent the characteristics or features of multi-dimensional objects such as words, images, etc.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

