\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f5\b \cf3 The in-memory mode
\f4\b0 \'a0is used for rapid testing, providing proof of concept (POC) and querying, allowing the reuse of collections between runs.\

\f5\b The persistent memory
\f4\b0 \'a0allows users to save and load data to and from a disk, causing the persistence of the database beyond the current session. This allows for the addition and deletion of documents after collection creation, and it is essential for production use cases where an in-memory database is not sufficient.\
Some of the key features of Chroma DB are:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
